{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_3","type":"mcp_tool_call","server":"tl-v1","tool":"ragflow_retrieval","arguments":{"dataset_ids":["d13efb7c8a9a11f197db2303d7337e37"],"metadata_condition":{"logic":"and","conditions":[{"name":"path","comparison_operator":"is","value":"sources"}]},"page_size":10,"vector_similarity_weight":0.3,"similarity_threshold":0.2,"top_k":1024,"keyword":false,"question":"\"large-file chunking\" Charlie September full large-file test corpus memory test stress case buffer release"},"result":{"content":[{"type":"text","text":"{\"chunks\": [{\"content\": \"**Source ID**: SRC-SLACK-44\\n\\n# Slack Thread: Large File Chunking Merge\\n\\n**Channel**: #cipherdoc\\n\\n**Thread opened**: 2026-08-16\\n\\n**Last activity**: 2026-08-20\\n\\n---\\n\\n**[2026-08-16 09:19] Charlie**: Merged the stream-chunking implementation into mainline. Calling this done.\\n\\n**[2026-08-16 09:21] Alice**: Great, this was overdue. Nice work.\\n\\n**[2026-08-16 09:57] Bob**: Anything left over from the memory concerns during testing, or is it fully clean?\\n\\n**[2026-08-16 10:00] Charlie**: As far as testing showed, clean. We'll see if anything shows up on longer runs.\\n\\n**[2026-08-20 09:01] Charlie**: Following up on the leak Bob found on the larger files — root cause was the chunk buffers not being explicitly released once a worker moved past them. Refactoring the buffer-release path now.\\n\\n**[2026-08-20 09:15] Bob**: Does the fix release eagerly after each chunk, or wait until the whole file finishes?\\n\\n**[2026-08-20 09:18] Charlie**: Eagerly, right after each chunk is processed — that's the whole point, don't let it accumulate. Still working through it, not ready to call it done again yet.\\n\\n**[2026-08-20 09:51] Diana**: Let me know when there's a build to re-run the stress case against.\\n\", \"content_ltks\": \"sourc id src slack 44 slack thread larg file chunk merg channel cipherdoc thread open 2026 08 16 last activ 2026 08 20 2026 08 16 09 19 charli merg the stream chunk implement into mainlin call this done 2026 08 16 09 21 alic great this wa overdu nice work 2026 08 16 09 57 bob anyth left over from the memori concern dure test or is it fulli clean 2026 08 16 1000 charli a far a test show clean we ll see if anyth show up on longer run 2026 08 20 09 01 charli follow up on the leak bob found on the larger file root caus wa the chunk buffer not be explicit releas onc a worker move past them refactor the buffer releas path now 2026 08 20 09 15 bob doe the fix releas eager after each chunk or wait until the whole file finish 2026 08 20 09 18 charli eager right after each chunk is process that s the whole point don t let it accumul still work through it not readi to call it done again yet 2026 08 20 09 51 diana let me know when there s a build to re run the stress case against\", \"dataset_id\": \"d13efb7c8a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"doc_type_kwd\": \"text\", \"document_id\": \"e8eb3f568a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"document_keyword\": \"med-synth/communication/sources/slack/2026-08-16-large-file-chunking-merge.md\", \"id\": \"eff9d8093fd3e4c5\", \"image_id\": \"\", \"important_keywords\": [], \"mom_id\": \"\", \"positions\": [], \"row_id\": null, \"similarity\": 0.37157017066899956, \"tag_kwd\": [], \"term_similarity\": 0.17004048666999938, \"vector_similarity\": 0.8418061, \"dataset_name\": \"C1Raw-2\", \"document_name\": \"med-synth/communication/sources/slack/2026-08-16-large-file-chunking-merge.md\", \"document_metadata\": {\"document_id\": \"e8eb3f568a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"name\": \"med-synth/communication/sources/slack/2026-08-16-large-file-chunking-merge.md\", \"location\": \"med-synth/communication/sources/slack/2026-08-16-large-file-chunking-merge.md\", \"type\": \"doc\", \"size\": 1195, \"chunk_count\": 1, \"create_date\": \"2026-07-28T23:42:16\", \"update_date\": \"2026-07-31T20:04:27\", \"token_count\": 363, \"thumbnail\": \"\", \"dataset_id\": \"d13efb7c8a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"meta_fields\": {\"path\": \"sources\"}}}, {\"content\": \"**Source ID**: SRC-GDOC-42\\n\\n# Design Review: Large-File Chunking — Post-Merge Reopen\\n\\n**Owner**: Charlie\\n\\n**Document Key**: DOC-2042\\n\\n**Last Updated**: 2026-08-23\\n\\n## Implemented Approach: Stream Chunking\\n\\nTo keep multi-GB PDFs from being loaded whole into memory, the redaction pipeline now streams large documents in fixed-size page chunks rather than holding the entire document in RAM. This implementation was merged to mainline on 2026-08-16.\\n\\n**Source ID**: SRC-GDOC-42\\n\\n# Design Review: Large-File Chunking — Post-Merge Reopen\\n\\n**Owner**: Charlie\\n\\n**Document Key**: DOC-2042\\n\\n**Last Updated**: 2026-08-23\\n\\n## Reopen: 2GB+ Leak\\n\\nPost-merge testing on files at and above 2GB surfaced a memory leak: buffers allocated for each chunk were not being released once the chunk finished processing, so peak memory climbed roughly linearly with file size instead of staying bounded by the chunk size. This defeated the point of chunking for the largest files, and the task was reopened as Active (Reopened).\\n\\n**Source ID**: SRC-GDOC-42\\n\\n# Design Review: Large-File Chunking — Post-Merge Reopen\\n\\n**Owner**: Charlie\\n\\n**Document Key**: DOC-2042\\n\\n**Last Updated**: 2026-08-23\\n\\n## In-Progress Fix: Per-Chunk Buffer Release\\n\\nCharlie is refactoring the stream-chunk handler to explicitly release each chunk's buffer once processing completes, rather than relying on it falling out of scope. Early local testing on a 2.3GB sample shows flat memory usage across chunks instead of the previous climb, but the fix has not yet been validated against the full large-file test corpus.\\n\\n*Status*: Chunking mechanism is in place and merged; buffer-release refactor to close the 2GB+ leak is still Active and not yet verified end-to-end.\\n\", \"content_ltks\": \"sourc id src gdoc 42 design review larg file chunk post merg reopen owner charli document key doc 2042 last updat 2026 08 23 implement approach stream chunk to keep multi gb pdfs from be load whole into memori the redact pipelin now stream larg document in fix size page chunk rather than hold the entir document in ram this implement wa merg to mainlin on 2026 08 16 sourc id src gdoc 42 design review larg file chunk post merg reopen owner charli document key doc 2042 last updat 2026 08 23 reopen 2gb leak post merg test on file at and abov 2gb surfac a memori leak buffer alloc for each chunk were not be releas onc the chunk finish process so peak memori climb rough linear with file size instead of stay bound by the chunk size this defeat the point of chunk for the largest file and the task wa reopen a activ reopen sourc id src gdoc 42 design review larg file chunk post merg reopen owner charli document key doc 2042 last updat 2026 08 23 in progress fix per chunk buffer releas charli is refactor the stream chunk handler to explicit releas each chunk s buffer onc process complet rather than reli on it fall out of scope earli local test on a2 3gb sampl show flat memori usag across chunk instead of the previous climb but the fix ha not yet been valid against the full larg file test corpus status chunk mechan is in place and merg buffer releas refactor to close the 2gb leak is still activ and not yet verifi end to end\", \"dataset_id\": \"d13efb7c8a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"doc_type_kwd\": \"text\", \"document_id\": \"e9ec20a08a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"document_keyword\": \"med-synth/documentation/sources/2026-08-23-Large-File-Chunking-Design-Review.md\", \"id\": \"dd6eaf806050ad34\", \"image_id\": \"\", \"important_keywords\": [], \"mom_id\": \"\", \"positions\": [], \"row_id\": null, \"similarity\": 0.3522076401975117, \"tag_kwd\": [], \"term_similarity\": 0.14979757171073108, \"vector_similarity\": 0.8244978, \"dataset_name\": \"C1Raw-2\", \"document_name\": \"med-synth/documentation/sources/2026-08-23-Large-File-Chunking-Design-Review.md\", \"document_metadata\": {\"document_id\": \"e9ec20a08a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"name\": \"med-synth/documentation/sources/2026-08-23-Large-File-Chunking-Design-Review.md\", \"location\": \"med-synth/documentation/sources/2026-08-23-Large-File-Chunking-Design-Review.md\", \"type\": \"doc\", \"size\": 1386, \"chunk_count\": 1, \"create_date\": \"2026-07-28T23:42:17\", \"update_date\": \"2026-07-31T20:00:46\", \"token_count\": 439, \"thumbnail\": \"\", \"dataset_id\": \"d13efb7c8a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"meta_fields\": {\"path\": \"sources\"}}}, {\"content\": \" - *Refactoring stream buffer release after each chunk after the task was reopened when files 2GB and larger were still found to leak memory.*\\n\", \"content_ltks\": \"refactor stream buffer releas after each chunk after the task wa reopen when file 2gb and larger were still found to leak memori\", \"dataset_id\": \"d13efb7c8a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"doc_type_kwd\": \"text\", \"document_id\": \"e96b7f688a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"document_keyword\": \"med-synth/tasks/CIPH-41-Large-File-Chunking.md\", \"id\": \"b70aca36f8ad3fb8\", \"image_id\": \"\", \"important_keywords\": [], \"mom_id\": \"\", \"positions\": [], \"row_id\": null, \"similarity\": 0.3349394053488337, \"tag_kwd\": [], \"term_similarity\": 0.11336032478404814, \"vector_similarity\": 0.85195726, \"dataset_name\": \"C1Raw-2\", \"document_name\": \"med-synth/tasks/CIPH-41-Large-File-Chunking.md\", \"document_metadata\": {\"document_id\": \"e96b7f688a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"name\": \"med-synth/tasks/CIPH-41-Large-File-Chunking.md\", \"location\": \"med-synth/tasks/CIPH-41-Large-File-Chunking.md\", \"type\": \"doc\", \"size\": 1122, \"chunk_count\": 2, \"create_date\": \"2026-07-28T23:42:17\", \"update_date\": \"2026-07-31T20:02:41\", \"token_count\": 577, \"thumbnail\": \"\", \"dataset_id\": \"d13efb7c8a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"meta_fields\": {\"path\": \"sources\"}}}, {\"content\": \"**Source ID**: SRC-GDOC-25\\n\\n# Design Note: Large File Chunking Strategy\\n\\n**Owner**: Charlie\\n\\n**Document Key**: DOC-2025\\n\\n**Last Updated**: 2026-08-14\\n\\n## The Failure Mode\\n\\nWhen processing massive multi-GB PDF documents (e.g., a 4,000-page merged archive), the loader attempts to load the entire document tree into RAM. For files exceeding 2GB, this consistently results in an `OOMKilled` exception in our standard 4GB Docker containers.\\n\\n**Source ID**: SRC-GDOC-25\\n\\n# Design Note: Large File Chunking Strategy\\n\\n**Owner**: Charlie\\n\\n**Document Key**: DOC-2025\\n\\n**Last Updated**: 2026-08-14\\n\\n## Chunking Implementation\\n\\nWe implemented and merged a \\\"Stream-and-Split\\\" pre-processing layer today. \\n\\n1. The CLI reads the source PDF in 100-page blocks.\\n\\n2. Each block is saved as a temporary sub-document (`doc_part_1.pdf`, `doc_part_2.pdf`).\\n\\n3. The worker pool processes these sub-documents independently.\\n\\n4. A post-processing step merges the redacted sub-documents back into a single final PDF.\\n\\n**Source ID**: SRC-GDOC-25\\n\\n# Design Note: Large File Chunking Strategy\\n\\n**Owner**: Charlie\\n\\n**Document Key**: DOC-2025\\n\\n**Last Updated**: 2026-08-14\\n\\n## Ordering and Memory Trade-off\\n\\nThis approach solves the RAM issue but introduces a significant disk I/O and ordering overhead. Re-merging the PDFs requires careful tracking of the chunk sequence. Furthermore, if a regex pattern was supposed to match across a page boundary (e.g., a sentence split across pages 100 and 101), the chunking will break the match. We are trading context-awareness for memory stability.\\n\\n*Pending*: We need to run a stress test with a 10,000-page document to verify if the final re-merge step (which also uses RAM) re-introduces the OOM crash.\\n\", \"content_ltks\": \"sourc id src gdoc 25 design note larg file chunk strategi owner charli document key doc 2025 last updat 2026 08 14 the failur mode when process massiv multi gb pdf document e g a4 000 page merg archiv the loader attempt to load the entir document tree into ram for file exceed 2gb this consist result in an oomkil except in our standard 4gb docker contain sourc id src gdoc 25 design note larg file chunk strategi owner charli document key doc 2025 last updat 2026 08 14 chunk implement we implement and merg a stream and split pre process layer today 1 the cli read the sourc pdf in 100 page block 2 each block is save a a temporari sub document doc _ part _ 1 pdf doc _ part _ 2 pdf 3 the worker pool process these sub document independ 4 a post process step merg the redact sub document back into a singl final pdf sourc id src gdoc 25 design note larg file chunk strategi owner charli document key doc 2025 last updat 2026 08 14 order and memori trade off this approach solv the ram issu but introduc a signific disk i o and order overhead re merg the pdfs requir care track of the chunk sequenc furthermor if a regex pattern wa suppos to match across a page boundari e g a sentenc split across page 100 and 101 the chunk will break the match we are trade context awar for memori stabil pend we need to run a stress test with a 10 000 page document to verifi if the final re merg step which also us ram re introduc the oom crash\", \"dataset_id\": \"d13efb7c8a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"doc_type_kwd\": \"text\", \"document_id\": \"e9af1e808a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"document_keyword\": \"med-synth/documentation/sources/2026-08-14-Large-File-Chunking-Review.md\", \"id\": \"a0395252cfde12bb\", \"image_id\": \"\", \"important_keywords\": [], \"mom_id\": \"\", \"positions\": [], \"row_id\": null, \"similarity\": 0.33334110163172637, \"tag_kwd\": [], \"term_similarity\": 0.12550607375960912, \"vector_similarity\": 0.8182895, \"dataset_name\": \"C1Raw-2\", \"document_name\": \"med-synth/documentation/sources/2026-08-14-Large-File-Chunking-Review.md\", \"document_metadata\": {\"document_id\": \"e9af1e808a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"name\": \"med-synth/documentation/sources/2026-08-14-Large-File-Chunking-Review.md\", \"location\": \"med-synth/documentation/sources/2026-08-14-Large-File-Chunking-Review.md\", \"type\": \"doc\", \"size\": 1406, \"chunk_count\": 1, \"create_date\": \"2026-07-28T23:42:17\", \"update_date\": \"2026-07-31T20:01:41\", \"token_count\": 447, \"thumbnail\": \"\", \"dataset_id\": \"d13efb7c8a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"meta_fields\": {\"path\": \"sources\"}}}, {\"content\": \"**Source ID**: SRC-SLACK-42\\n\\n# Slack Thread: Large File Chunking\\n\\n**Channel**: #cipherdoc\\n\\n**Date**: 2026-08-14\\n\\n---\\n\\n**[2026-08-14 11:30] Charlie**: Starting on stream-based chunked reads for large PDFs. Loading the whole document into memory before redacting is what's causing the pressure on bigger files.\\n\\n**[2026-08-14 11:32] Bob**: Makes sense. What's the plan for entities that span a chunk boundary — like an address that gets split across two reads?\\n\\n**[2026-08-14 11:58] Charlie**: Adding a small overlap window between chunks so anything near a boundary gets caught on both sides instead of falling through the gap.\\n\\n**[2026-08-14 11:59] Alice**: Does this help or hurt the multi-threading work?\\n\\n**[2026-08-14 12:04] Charlie**: Should help — lower memory per worker means we're not as constrained on how many workers we can run at once.\\n\\n**[2026-08-14 12:22] Bob**: Good. Let me know when it's ready for a real large-file test.\\n\", \"content_ltks\": \"sourc id src slack 42 slack thread larg file chunk channel cipherdoc date 2026 08 14 2026 08 14 11 30 charli start on stream base chunk read for larg pdfs load the whole document into memori befor redact is what s caus the pressur on bigger file 2026 08 14 11 32 bob make sens what s the plan for entiti that span a chunk boundari like an address that get split across two read 2026 08 14 11 58 charli ad a small overlap window between chunk so anyth near a boundari get caught on both side instead of fall through the gap 2026 08 14 11 59 alic doe this help or hurt the multi thread work 2026 08 14 12 04 charli should help lower memori per worker mean we re not a constrain on how mani worker we can run at onc 2026 08 14 12 22 bob good let me know when it s readi for a real larg file test\", \"dataset_id\": \"d13efb7c8a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"doc_type_kwd\": \"text\", \"document_id\": \"e8dbc5b28a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"document_keyword\": \"med-synth/communication/sources/slack/2026-08-14-large-file-chunking.md\", \"id\": \"f9df4a58ad5dbafe\", \"image_id\": \"\", \"important_keywords\": [], \"mom_id\": \"\", \"positions\": [], \"row_id\": null, \"similarity\": 0.32533478725453613, \"tag_kwd\": [], \"term_similarity\": 0.1093117417921945, \"vector_similarity\": 0.82938856, \"dataset_name\": \"C1Raw-2\", \"document_name\": \"med-synth/communication/sources/slack/2026-08-14-large-file-chunking.md\", \"document_metadata\": {\"document_id\": \"e8dbc5b28a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"name\": \"med-synth/communication/sources/slack/2026-08-14-large-file-chunking.md\", \"location\": \"med-synth/communication/sources/slack/2026-08-14-large-file-chunking.md\", \"type\": \"doc\", \"size\": 942, \"chunk_count\": 1, \"create_date\": \"2026-07-28T23:42:16\", \"update_date\": \"2026-07-31T20:04:39\", \"token_count\": 280, \"thumbnail\": \"\", \"dataset_id\": \"d13efb7c8a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"meta_fields\": {\"path\": \"sources\"}}}, {\"content\": \"**Source ID**: SRC-SLACK-43\\n\\n# Slack Thread: Large File Chunking Reopen\\n\\n**Channel**: #cipherdoc\\n\\n**Date**: 2026-08-18\\n\\n---\\n\\n**[2026-08-18 10:30] Bob**: Reopening large-file chunking. On long-running batches with files over 2GB, memory is still leaking even though the chunked-read path is supposedly done.\\n\\n**[2026-08-18 10:31] Charlie**: That's odd, chunking should mean each buffer gets dropped once we move past it.\\n\\n**[2026-08-18 10:41] Bob**: It's not the page buffers themselves — something else is holding a reference and keeping them from being freed.\\n\\n**[2026-08-18 11:08] Diana**: I can reproduce it in QA too. Memory climbs steadily and the process eventually gets killed on the larger inputs.\\n\\n**[2026-08-18 11:20] Charlie**: I'll dig into what's still holding those references. Reopening this until we find it.\\n\", \"content_ltks\": \"sourc id src slack 43 slack thread larg file chunk reopen channel cipherdoc date 2026 08 18 2026 08 18 10 30 bob reopen larg file chunk on long run batch with file over 2gb memori is still leak even though the chunk read path is suppos done 2026 08 18 10 31 charli that s odd chunk should mean each buffer get drop onc we move past it 2026 08 18 10 41 bob it s not the page buffer themselv someth els is hold a refer and keep them from be freed 2026 08 18 11 08 diana i can reproduc it in qa too memori climb steadili and the process eventu get kill on the larger input 2026 08 18 11 20 charli i ll dig into what s still hold those refer reopen this until we find it\", \"dataset_id\": \"d13efb7c8a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"doc_type_kwd\": \"text\", \"document_id\": \"e91bada88a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"document_keyword\": \"med-synth/communication/sources/slack/2026-08-18-large-file-chunking-reopen.md\", \"id\": \"e5e49e8fd5982668\", \"image_id\": \"\", \"important_keywords\": [], \"mom_id\": \"\", \"positions\": [], \"row_id\": null, \"similarity\": 0.320833102065941, \"tag_kwd\": [], \"term_similarity\": 0.10121457580848717, \"vector_similarity\": 0.83327633, \"dataset_name\": \"C1Raw-2\", \"document_name\": \"med-synth/communication/sources/slack/2026-08-18-large-file-chunking-reopen.md\", \"document_metadata\": {\"document_id\": \"e91bada88a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"name\": \"med-synth/communication/sources/slack/2026-08-18-large-file-chunking-reopen.md\", \"location\": \"med-synth/communication/sources/slack/2026-08-18-large-file-chunking-reopen.md\", \"type\": \"doc\", \"size\": 825, \"chunk_count\": 1, \"create_date\": \"2026-07-28T23:42:16\", \"update_date\": \"2026-07-31T20:03:48\", \"token_count\": 252, \"thumbnail\": \"\", \"dataset_id\": \"d13efb7c8a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"meta_fields\": {\"path\": \"sources\"}}}, {\"content\": \"# ClickUp Task: CIPH-41\\n\\n**Source ID**: SRC-CU-CIPH-41\\n\\n**Task ID**: CIPH-41\\n\\n**Title**: Stream-chunk multi-GB PDF loads without retaining buffers\\n\\n**Status**: Active (Reopened)\\n\\n**Assignee**: Charlie\\n\\n**Priority**: Normal\\n\\n**Date Created**: 2026-08-12\\n\\n## Description\\n\\nAdd stream chunking so large, multi-GB PDF documents can be processed without excessive memory pressure. Chunking was merged, but the task was reopened after files over 2GB were found to still leak memory; buffer-release logic is being refactored to release buffers after each chunk.\\n\\n# ClickUp Task: CIPH-41\\n\\n**Source ID**: SRC-CU-CIPH-41\\n\\n**Task ID**: CIPH-41\\n\\n**Title**: Stream-chunk multi-GB PDF loads without retaining buffers\\n\\n**Status**: Active (Reopened)\\n\\n**Assignee**: Charlie\\n\\n**Priority**: Normal\\n\\n**Date Created**: 2026-08-12\\n\\n## Acceptance Criteria\\n\\n- Large PDF documents are processed via stream chunking rather than loading whole files into memory.\\n\\n- Memory buffers are released after each chunk, with no leak on files 2GB and larger.\\n\\n# ClickUp Task: CIPH-41\\n\\n**Source ID**: SRC-CU-CIPH-41\\n\\n**Task ID**: CIPH-41\\n\\n**Title**: Stream-chunk multi-GB PDF loads without retaining buffers\\n\\n**Status**: Active (Reopened)\\n\\n**Assignee**: Charlie\\n\\n**Priority**: Normal\\n\\n**Date Created**: 2026-08-12\\n\\n## Description\\n\\nAdd stream chunking so large, multi-GB PDF documents can be processed without excessive memory pressure. Chunking was merged, but the task was reopened after files over 2GB were found to still leak memory; buffer-release logic is being refactored to release buffers after each chunk.\\n\\n# ClickUp Task: CIPH-41\\n\\n**Source ID**: SRC-CU-CIPH-41\\n\\n**Task ID**: CIPH-41\\n\\n**Title**: Stream-chunk multi-GB PDF loads without retaining buffers\\n\\n**Status**: Active (Reopened)\\n\\n**Assignee**: Charlie\\n\\n**Priority**: Normal\\n\\n**Date Created**: 2026-08-12\\n\\n## Activity History\\n\\n- **2026-08-12**: Alice - Task Create (Open)\\n\\n - *Opened the task because large-file chunking is needed for multi-GB documents.*\\n\\n- **2026-08-20**: Charlie - Buffer Release Refactor (Active (Reopened))\\n\", \"content_ltks\": \"clickup task ciph 41 sourc id src cu ciph 41 task id ciph 41 titl stream chunk multi gb pdf load without retain buffer status activ reopen assigne charli prioriti normal date creat 2026 08 12 descript add stream chunk so larg multi gb pdf document can be process without excess memori pressur chunk wa merg but the task wa reopen after file over 2gb were found to still leak memori buffer releas logic is be refactor to releas buffer after each chunk clickup task ciph 41 sourc id src cu ciph 41 task id ciph 41 titl stream chunk multi gb pdf load without retain buffer status activ reopen assigne charli prioriti normal date creat 2026 08 12 accept criterion larg pdf document are process via stream chunk rather than load whole file into memori memori buffer are releas after each chunk with no leak on file 2gb and larger clickup task ciph 41 sourc id src cu ciph 41 task id ciph 41 titl stream chunk multi gb pdf load without retain buffer status activ reopen assigne charli prioriti normal date creat 2026 08 12 descript add stream chunk so larg multi gb pdf document can be process without excess memori pressur chunk wa merg but the task wa reopen after file over 2gb were found to still leak memori buffer releas logic is be refactor to releas buffer after each chunk clickup task ciph 41 sourc id src cu ciph 41 task id ciph 41 titl stream chunk multi gb pdf load without retain buffer status activ reopen assigne charli prioriti normal date creat 2026 08 12 activ histori 2026 08 12 alic task creat open open the task becaus larg file chunk is need for multi gb document 2026 08 20 charli buffer releas refactor activ reopen\", \"dataset_id\": \"d13efb7c8a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"doc_type_kwd\": \"text\", \"document_id\": \"e96b7f688a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"document_keyword\": \"med-synth/tasks/CIPH-41-Large-File-Chunking.md\", \"id\": \"7fab92c2892cd73f\", \"image_id\": \"\", \"important_keywords\": [], \"mom_id\": \"\", \"positions\": [], \"row_id\": null, \"similarity\": 0.3206421182545361, \"tag_kwd\": [], \"term_similarity\": 0.10931174179219448, \"vector_similarity\": 0.81374633, \"dataset_name\": \"C1Raw-2\", \"document_name\": \"med-synth/tasks/CIPH-41-Large-File-Chunking.md\", \"document_metadata\": {\"document_id\": \"e96b7f688a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"name\": \"med-synth/tasks/CIPH-41-Large-File-Chunking.md\", \"location\": \"med-synth/tasks/CIPH-41-Large-File-Chunking.md\", \"type\": \"doc\", \"size\": 1122, \"chunk_count\": 2, \"create_date\": \"2026-07-28T23:42:17\", \"update_date\": \"2026-07-31T20:02:41\", \"token_count\": 577, \"thumbnail\": \"\", \"dataset_id\": \"d13efb7c8a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"meta_fields\": {\"path\": \"sources\"}}}, {\"content\": \"**Source ID**: SRC-GDOC-44\\n\\n# Profiling Report: PDF Loader Memory Leak — Tracemalloc Patch\\n\\n**Owner**: Bob\\n\\n**Document Key**: DOC-2044\\n\\n**Last Updated**: 2026-08-23\\n\\n## Trigger\\n\\nProfiling was opened after the T031 large-file chunking reopen surfaced memory growth on 2GB+ documents; the team wanted to confirm whether the loader itself, separate from the chunk-buffer issue being fixed under T031, was also retaining memory it shouldn't.\\n\\n**Source ID**: SRC-GDOC-44\\n\\n# Profiling Report: PDF Loader Memory Leak — Tracemalloc Patch\\n\\n**Owner**: Bob\\n\\n**Document Key**: DOC-2044\\n\\n**Last Updated**: 2026-08-23\\n\\n## Tooling Constraint\\n\\nThe offline lab environment does not have the team's usual commercial profiler available (network-gated license check), so profiling switched to Python's stdlib `tracemalloc`, which works fully offline.\\n\\n**Source ID**: SRC-GDOC-44\\n\\n# Profiling Report: PDF Loader Memory Leak — Tracemalloc Patch\\n\\n**Owner**: Bob\\n\\n**Document Key**: DOC-2044\\n\\n**Last Updated**: 2026-08-23\\n\\n## Findings and Patch\\n\\nTracemalloc traced the retained allocations to the PDF loader's internal page-object cache, which was holding references to fully-parsed page objects long after the redaction pass for that page had completed. Bob patched the loader to explicitly drop the cache entry once a page's redaction pass finishes, rather than waiting for document close.\\n\\n**Source ID**: SRC-GDOC-44\\n\\n# Profiling Report: PDF Loader Memory Leak — Tracemalloc Patch\\n\\n**Owner**: Bob\\n\\n**Document Key**: DOC-2044\\n\\n**Last Updated**: 2026-08-23\\n\\n## Validation\\n\\nRe-ran the same profiling pass post-patch: peak memory during a 2GB+ document run dropped to match the chunk-bounded footprint expected from the T031 chunking work, confirming the loader-side leak — distinct from the T031 buffer-release issue — is resolved.\\n\\n*Status*: Completed. Loader-side leak patched and verified; result depends on and complements the T031 chunking/buffer-release fix.\\n\", \"content_ltks\": \"sourc id src gdoc 44 profil report pdf loader memori leak tracemalloc patch owner bob document key doc 2044 last updat 2026 08 23 trigger profil wa open after the t031 larg file chunk reopen surfac memori growth on 2gb document the team want to confirm whether the loader itself separ from the chunk buffer issu be fix under t031 wa also retain memori it shouldn t sourc id src gdoc 44 profil report pdf loader memori leak tracemalloc patch owner bob document key doc 2044 last updat 2026 08 23 tool constraint the offlin lab environ doe not have the team s usual commerci profil avail network gate licens check so profil switch to python s stdlib tracemalloc which work fulli offlin sourc id src gdoc 44 profil report pdf loader memori leak tracemalloc patch owner bob document key doc 2044 last updat 2026 08 23 find and patch tracemalloc trace the retain alloc to the pdf loader s intern page object cach which wa hold refer to fulli pars page object long after the redact pas for that page had complet bob patch the loader to explicit drop the cach entri onc a page s redact pas finish rather than wait for document close sourc id src gdoc 44 profil report pdf loader memori leak tracemalloc patch owner bob document key doc 2044 last updat 2026 08 23 valid re ran the same profil pas post patch peak memori dure a 2gb document run drop to match the chunk bound footprint expect from the t031 chunk work confirm the loader side leak distinct from the t031 buffer releas issu is resolv status complet loader side leak patch and verifi result depend on and complement the t031 chunk buffer releas fix\", \"dataset_id\": \"d13efb7c8a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"doc_type_kwd\": \"text\", \"document_id\": \"e9df68608a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"document_keyword\": \"med-synth/documentation/sources/2026-08-23-Memory-Leak-Profiling-Report.md\", \"id\": \"f22e8883670ff4bd\", \"image_id\": \"\", \"important_keywords\": [], \"mom_id\": \"\", \"positions\": [], \"row_id\": null, \"similarity\": 0.2994383642545361, \"tag_kwd\": [], \"term_similarity\": 0.10931174179219448, \"vector_similarity\": 0.74306715, \"dataset_name\": \"C1Raw-2\", \"document_name\": \"med-synth/documentation/sources/2026-08-23-Memory-Leak-Profiling-Report.md\", \"document_metadata\": {\"document_id\": \"e9df68608a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"name\": \"med-synth/documentation/sources/2026-08-23-Memory-Leak-Profiling-Report.md\", \"location\": \"med-synth/documentation/sources/2026-08-23-Memory-Leak-Profiling-Report.md\", \"type\": \"doc\", \"size\": 1441, \"chunk_count\": 1, \"create_date\": \"2026-07-28T23:42:17\", \"update_date\": \"2026-07-31T20:01:00\", \"token_count\": 490, \"thumbnail\": \"\", \"dataset_id\": \"d13efb7c8a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"meta_fields\": {\"path\": \"sources\"}}}, {\"content\": \"**Source ID**: SRC-SLACK-49\\n\\n# Slack Thread: Memory Leak Tracemalloc Patch\\n\\n**Channel**: #cipherdoc\\n\\n**Thread opened**: 2026-08-21\\n\\n**Last activity**: 2026-08-23\\n\\n---\\n\\n**[2026-08-21 09:00] Charlie**: Switching to `tracemalloc` for the leak hunt since the usual profiler is a no-go on the offline lab box. Kicking off a fresh capture now.\\n\\n**[2026-08-21 11:05] Charlie**: Already got something. The `tracemalloc` output shows we're holding onto the full page-tree in `RedactionEngine` even after the document object is closed.\\n\\n**[2026-08-21 11:50] Bob**: That lines up with the hotspot list from earlier this week. I'll start on a patch tonight.\\n\\n**[2026-08-23 09:45] Bob**: Patch is in. Added explicit cleanup so the context manager actually releases the page-tree reference instead of just closing the file handle.\\n\\n**[2026-08-23 09:47] Diana**: Just finished a 6-hour soak test with the new build. Memory usage is flat as a pancake after the initial load. :pancake:\\n\\n**[2026-08-23 10:41] Alice**: Huge relief. Is this on top of the buffer-release fix from the large-file chunking rework, or a separate code path?\\n\\n**[2026-08-23 10:43] Bob**: Same family of fix — builds on the chunking buffer-release work. PR #84 is merged.\\n\\n**[2026-08-23 10:44] Evan**: On it.\\n\\n**[2026-08-23 10:46] Evan**: Rolling this out to the dev clusters. @Charlie thanks for the tracemalloc deep dive.\\n\", \"content_ltks\": \"sourc id src slack 49 slack thread memori leak tracemalloc patch channel cipherdoc thread open 2026 08 21 last activ 2026 08 23 2026 08 21 09 00 charli switch to tracemalloc for the leak hunt sinc the usual profil is a no go on the offlin lab box kick off a fresh captur now 2026 08 21 11 05 charli alreadi got someth the tracemalloc output show we re hold onto the full page tree in redactionengin even after the document object is close 2026 08 21 11 50 bob that line up with the hotspot list from earlier this week i ll start on a patch tonight 2026 08 23 09 45 bob patch is in ad explicit cleanup so the context manag actual releas the page tree refer instead of just close the file handl 2026 08 23 09 47 diana just finish a 6 hour soak test with the new build memori usag is flat a a pancak after the initi load pancak 2026 08 23 10 41 alic huge relief is this on top of the buffer releas fix from the larg file chunk rework or a separ code path 2026 08 23 10 43 bob same famili of fix build on the chunk buffer releas work pr 84 is merg 2026 08 23 10 44 evan on it 2026 08 23 10 46 evan roll this out to the dev cluster charli thank for the tracemalloc deep dive\", \"dataset_id\": \"d13efb7c8a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"doc_type_kwd\": \"text\", \"document_id\": \"e8e281228a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"document_keyword\": \"med-synth/communication/sources/slack/2026-08-21-memory-leak-tracemalloc.md\", \"id\": \"824fb66730068003\", \"image_id\": \"\", \"important_keywords\": [], \"mom_id\": \"\", \"positions\": [], \"row_id\": null, \"similarity\": 0.2968365899716434, \"tag_kwd\": [], \"term_similarity\": 0.09716599281663352, \"vector_similarity\": 0.76273465, \"dataset_name\": \"C1Raw-2\", \"document_name\": \"med-synth/communication/sources/slack/2026-08-21-memory-leak-tracemalloc.md\", \"document_metadata\": {\"document_id\": \"e8e281228a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"name\": \"med-synth/communication/sources/slack/2026-08-21-memory-leak-tracemalloc.md\", \"location\": \"med-synth/communication/sources/slack/2026-08-21-memory-leak-tracemalloc.md\", \"type\": \"doc\", \"size\": 1379, \"chunk_count\": 1, \"create_date\": \"2026-07-28T23:42:16\", \"update_date\": \"2026-07-31T20:04:34\", \"token_count\": 428, \"thumbnail\": \"\", \"dataset_id\": \"d13efb7c8a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"meta_fields\": {\"path\": \"sources\"}}}, {\"content\": \"**Source ID**: SRC-GDOC-27\\n\\n# Document: Memory-Leak-Hotspot-Identification-Review\\n\\n**Owner**: Bob\\n\\n**Document Key**: DOC-2027\\n\\n**Last Updated**: 2026-08-27 (retrospective, covers 2026-08-17)\\n\\n## Decision Notes\\n\\nAnalysis of memory consumption patterns in the redaction engine, targeting long-running batch processes. This review was triggered by signals from the large-file stream chunking rework.\\n\\n**Source ID**: SRC-GDOC-27\\n\\n# Document: Memory-Leak-Hotspot-Identification-Review\\n\\n**Owner**: Bob\\n\\n**Document Key**: DOC-2027\\n\\n**Last Updated**: 2026-08-27 (retrospective, covers 2026-08-17)\\n\\n## Identification and Profiling Findings\\n\\nBob began identifying leak hotspots in the PDF loader on 2026-08-17. The standard profiler tooling normally used for this kind of investigation was not available in the offline lab environment, which blocked progress for a few days until Charlie switched the approach to Python's stdlib `tracemalloc` on 2026-08-21. Tracing allocations during a chunked large-file run with tracemalloc pointed to the PDF loader's page-buffer handling as the source of retained allocations across chunk boundaries — buffers that should have been released between chunks were staying reachable.\\n\\n**Source ID**: SRC-GDOC-27\\n\\n# Document: Memory-Leak-Hotspot-Identification-Review\\n\\n**Owner**: Bob\\n\\n**Document Key**: DOC-2027\\n\\n**Last Updated**: 2026-08-27 (retrospective, covers 2026-08-17)\\n\\n## Scope of this note\\n\\nThis note covers only the identification pass: where the leak signal traces to and how it was found. Patching the loader is separate follow-up work and is not reported on here.\\n\", \"content_ltks\": \"sourc id src gdoc 27 document memori leak hotspot identif review owner bob document key doc 2027 last updat 2026 08 27 retrospect cover 2026 08 17 decis note analysi of memori consumpt pattern in the redact engin target long run batch process this review wa trigger by signal from the larg file stream chunk rework sourc id src gdoc 27 document memori leak hotspot identif review owner bob document key doc 2027 last updat 2026 08 27 retrospect cover 2026 08 17 identif and profil find bob began identifi leak hotspot in the pdf loader on 2026 08 17 the standard profil tool normal use for this kind of investig wa not avail in the offlin lab environ which block progress for a few day until charli switch the approach to python s stdlib tracemalloc on 2026 08 21 trace alloc dure a chunk larg file run with tracemalloc point to the pdf loader s page buffer handl a the sourc of retain alloc across chunk boundari buffer that should have been releas between chunk were stay reachabl sourc id src gdoc 27 document memori leak hotspot identif review owner bob document key doc 2027 last updat 2026 08 27 retrospect cover 2026 08 17 scope of this note this note cover onli the identif pas where the leak signal trace to and how it wa found patch the loader is separ follow up work and is not report on here\", \"dataset_id\": \"d13efb7c8a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"doc_type_kwd\": \"text\", \"document_id\": \"e9cacd928a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"document_keyword\": \"med-synth/documentation/sources/2026-08-27-Memory-Leak-Profiling-Review.md\", \"id\": \"92bea1ebb85612d0\", \"image_id\": \"\", \"important_keywords\": [], \"mom_id\": \"\", \"positions\": [], \"row_id\": null, \"similarity\": 0.2932517099716434, \"tag_kwd\": [], \"term_similarity\": 0.0971659928166335, \"vector_similarity\": 0.75078505, \"dataset_name\": \"C1Raw-2\", \"document_name\": \"med-synth/documentation/sources/2026-08-27-Memory-Leak-Profiling-Review.md\", \"document_metadata\": {\"document_id\": \"e9cacd928a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"name\": \"med-synth/documentation/sources/2026-08-27-Memory-Leak-Profiling-Review.md\", \"location\": \"med-synth/documentation/sources/2026-08-27-Memory-Leak-Profiling-Review.md\", \"type\": \"doc\", \"size\": 1213, \"chunk_count\": 1, \"create_date\": \"2026-07-28T23:42:17\", \"update_date\": \"2026-07-31T20:01:16\", \"token_count\": 416, \"thumbnail\": \"\", \"dataset_id\": \"d13efb7c8a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"meta_fields\": {\"path\": \"sources\"}}}], \"pagination\": {\"page\": 1, \"page_size\": 10, \"total_chunks\": 70, \"total_pages\": 7}, \"query_info\": {\"question\": \"\\\"large-file chunking\\\" Charlie September full large-file test corpus memory test stress case buffer release\", \"similarity_threshold\": 0.2, \"vector_weight\": 0.3, \"keyword_search\": false, \"dataset_count\": 1}}"}],"structured_content":null},"error":null,"status":"completed"}}
